1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,008
PACT. The AI Payment Guardian.

2
00:00:03,008 --> 00:00:08,104
Give AI the power to act, not unrestricted access to your money.

3
00:00:12,483 --> 00:00:14,622
AI agents can now shop for us.

4
00:00:14,622 --> 00:00:18,281
But to pay, we hand them a payment method with no limits.

5
00:00:18,281 --> 00:00:21,658
One injected instruction, or one hallucinated price,

6
00:00:21,658 --> 00:00:25,004
and real money moves before anyone approves it.

7
00:00:32,517 --> 00:00:35,384
PACT sits between the agent and PayPal.

8
00:00:35,384 --> 00:00:37,459
The AI can only recommend.

9
00:00:37,459 --> 00:00:40,449
A deterministic policy engine authorizes,

10
00:00:40,449 --> 00:00:43,506
a human approves, and PayPal executes.

11
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:46,794
It starts with a spending mandate.

12
00:00:46,794 --> 00:00:49,937
This one allows electronics from one merchant,

13
00:00:49,937 --> 00:00:52,049
up to $100 per purchase.

14
00:00:52,883 --> 00:00:56,745
Now the agent is asked for a keyboard that costs $125.

15
00:00:56,745 --> 00:00:58,552
Gemini recommends it,

16
00:00:58,552 --> 00:01:01,916
and the policy engine answers immediately.

17
00:01:02,750 --> 00:01:05,969
Blocked. Attempted $125. Allowed $100.

18
00:01:05,969 --> 00:01:09,818
There is no approve button and no PayPal order.

19
00:01:09,818 --> 00:01:12,617
The AI can recommend a purchase,

20
00:01:12,617 --> 00:01:16,995
but it cannot override the user's spending mandate.

21
00:01:17,850 --> 00:01:20,220
Next, an eligible request.

22
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:24,403
Gemini picks an $89 keyboard, and every rule passes.

23
00:01:24,403 --> 00:01:27,999
But passing policy is not authorization.

24
00:01:28,850 --> 00:01:30,563
I review the budget impact,

25
00:01:30,563 --> 00:01:32,569
then approve this exact purchase.

26
00:01:32,569 --> 00:01:34,771
My approval is bound to a fingerprint

27
00:01:34,771 --> 00:01:37,468
of the product, the price and the mandate.

28
00:01:38,317 --> 00:01:40,920
PACT creates a real PayPal Sandbox order,

29
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:43,986
and the buyer approves it in PayPal Checkout.

30
00:01:44,850 --> 00:01:47,582
Back in PACT, the server asks PayPal directly

31
00:01:47,582 --> 00:01:49,387
whether the buyer approved.

32
00:01:49,387 --> 00:01:52,009
Only then can the payment be captured.

33
00:01:52,850 --> 00:01:54,097
Captured.

34
00:01:54,097 --> 00:01:57,839
A real PayPal capture ID, status COMPLETED,

35
00:01:57,839 --> 00:01:59,850
for exactly $89.

36
00:02:00,716 --> 00:02:03,412
What if something changes after approval?

37
00:02:03,412 --> 00:02:05,392
I approve a second keyboard.

38
00:02:05,392 --> 00:02:08,007
Then the merchant raises the price.

39
00:02:08,850 --> 00:02:10,949
The approval is void at once.

40
00:02:10,949 --> 00:02:14,604
A change can never silently inherit an old approval.

41
00:02:15,450 --> 00:02:18,098
Every step is recorded in the audit trail:

42
00:02:18,098 --> 00:02:20,640
the recommendation, the policy decision,

43
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:23,804
the approval, the PayPal order and the capture.

44
00:02:24,650 --> 00:02:28,920
AI recommends. The policy engine authorizes.

45
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:32,368
A human approves. PayPal executes.

46
00:02:32,368 --> 00:02:35,739
PACT. The AI Payment Guardian.
